        "description": "Before dispatching a search for a specific object, confirm that the object type is present and coolable. If the object is not found after a reasonable search, consider that the task may be impossible and report failure early. Treat an empty exhaustive search as evidence the object may be absent and avoid repeating identical SEARCH missions."
      }
    },
    {
      "op": "UPDATE",
      "target_role": "Supervisor",
      "target_skill_id": "skill_017",
      "evidence_ref": "stage2-local-v10-role-partitioned-patch3/generation_02/client_C/episode_132",
      "patch": {
        "principle": "For 双物品放置 tasks, treat the mission as two independent search-and-place cycles: locate and take the first target object, place it at the destination, then locate and take the second target object and place it at the destination. Track placed-item state and search elsewhere for the second instance; do not dispatch a search to take an object already at the destination."
      }
    }
